  "note": "Election of 15 members of Portrush Urban District Council on 18 May 1949; the result was declared at 3 a.m. the next day. No party labels are printed in the result; asterisks mark sitting members as printed. Twenty-four candidates were nominated and none withdrew (Belfast News-Letter, 5 May 1949, p. 3; Irish News, 6 May 1949, p. 3); the nine not elected are entered from the nomination list without votes, which the paper does not print. The nomination list marks nominees of the Ratepayers' Association '(R.A.)', among them the elected R. B. Adams, Buchanan, Traynor and Mason. Losers not printed: re-checked on the British Newspaper Archive's page image of the Belfast News-Letter, 19 May 1949, p. 5 (13 Nov 2026): the paper lists the fifteen elected with their votes only.",
  "losersNotPrinted": true,
  "correctionNote": "Corrected from the page images of the Belfast News-Letter, 19 May 1949, p. 5, and 5 May 1949, p. 3 (council-audit, Nov 2026): the nine defeated candidates of the 24 nominated are now entered, without votes (none are printed)."
